From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: notify PPE after returning DS TX buffers

After recycling a nonempty TX completion batch, notify the native PPE
transport that its TX buffer pool can refill a stalled RXFILL ring. Call
outside the WLAN pool and SRNG locks and only for successful returns,
retaining the existing fault checks and batched index synchronization.
Keep PPDU, monitor, rate and airtime statistics unchanged.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>

Adapted from JiaY-shi/flint3e-support 89783319734e683acde27509c401d163f6319e7a.
Retain the local VP lifecycle and AHB RX completion/refill protections.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/ppe_ds.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/ppe_ds.c
@@ -635,8 +635,11 @@ bad_cookie:
 		dev_put(dev);
 	}
 	ath12k_ds_flush_rx(ds);
-	if (ds->handle && !READ_ONCE(ds->faulted))
+	if (ds->handle && !READ_ONCE(ds->faulted)) {
 		qcom_ppe_ds_sync(ds->handle);
+		if (completed)
+			qcom_ppe_ds_refill_ready(ds->handle);
+	}
 	if (READ_ONCE(ds->faulted))
 		ath12k_ds_fault(ds);
 	return (done + 3) >> 2;
